- op: discuss  # 35ca
  at: '2026-09-20T21:16:51Z'  # 35ca
  by: agent  # 35ca
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 35ca
  clock: 9  # 35ca
  nonce: 35ca  # 35ca
  message: "SHIPPED as PR #1105 (dev dead90232c), owner-merged under the governance gate. All three approved parts.\n\nA -- auto-pr traps TERM/INT/HUP behind ONE _autopr_install_traps boundary (replacing three hand-written trap blocks) and records terminated_sigterm / terminated_sigint / terminated_sighup: a FOURTH bucket, folded into neither convergence nor failure. Two rules are load-bearing and each has a test: a signal NEVER overwrites a state the run already declared (a kill during post-merge housekeeping must not rewrite a landed merge -- that is Class 1 with the sign flipped), and the signal is recorded EITHER WAY in its own `terminated_by` field, which is exactly the fact Class 1's investigation had to recover from a surviving terminal log.\n\nB -- audit-autopr-convergence reads the bucket without laundering it: a terminated run is disclosed but counted neither way, a converged verdict names its DECIDING denominator, an all-kills ledger is CANNOT CONCLUDE, and undeclared rows predating the traps are reported as UNATTRIBUTABLE.\n\nC -- AGENTS.md carries the budget arithmetic and nohup-detached as the agent shape, with \"never wrap auto-pr in timeout\".\n\nLIVE EVIDENCE on this fix's own PR. The #1105 run's sentinel:\n    {\"exit_code\": 0, \"final_state\": \"governance_pending\", \"terminated_by\": null, ...}\nThe field is in production and null on an unsignalled run -- the third value (not signalled), distinct from the ABSENT key on a pre-fix row. 8 new behavioral tests; 2341 passed in the affected slice.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, so closure is not mistaken for completeness. The audit's verdict on the real ledger is UNCHANGED -- still VIOLATION, 77 runs -- because historical rows cannot be reclassified: the fact was never recorded. Attribution starts from the next run. INV-rahib stays violated.\n\nTWO FIXTURE ERRORS WORTH KEEPING, both caught by the tests rather than by review.\n(1) The first draft blocked with `sleep 60`. Bash defers a trap until its foreground child exits, so the fixture sat on the signal for 60s and read as \"the trap never fired\". Production polls on SHORT sleeps, so the faithful fixture is a loop of `sleep 0.1` -- the harness has to match the shape of the thing it models, not just its flags (the same lesson as reading production's `set` line instead of retyping it).\n(2) An audit assertion demanded `VERDICT: CONVERGED` be ABSENT on an all-kills ledger, which contradicted the rule written beside it. The right rule is that no decisions means no evidence: CANNOT CONCLUDE.\n\nThe ergonomics half is filed as WI-hajak (auto-pr --detach). Status -> done."  # 35ca
